VERDICT: REJECTED
The diff does not meet the task’s core requirement that game state be reliably scoped to the authenticated active character; there are blocking cross-character data integrity issues.

Critical findings:
- **Global destructive delete remains in multi-user mode**: `DELETE /character` in `routes/character.ts` still deletes entire tables without `characterId` filters (`inventory`, `skills`, `characters`, etc.). Any one user can wipe all players’ data.
- **State leakage across characters still present**:
  - `routes/character.ts` uses unscoped reads like `combatStateTable.limit(1)`, `heroicStateTable.limit(1)`, and AA node load (`aaPointsTable` by rank only) instead of filtering by active character.
  - `lib/skillXp.ts` still applies XP by `skillId` only (no `characterId`), so meditation XP can land on the wrong character/account.
